Q. What is Spring Boot auto-configuration and how does it work internally?
Ans: 
Auto - Configuration Means:
	- Auto configuration is the feature of spring boot that automatically configures 
	  your application based on the dependencies present in the classpath.
	- Suppose your application has spring boot starter web dependency then spring boot 
	  will automatically
		a. configure DispatcherServlet
		b. start embedded Tomcat
		c. Set up Spring MVC
		d. Configure JSON support (Jackson)
	- You don't need to write configuration manually.

How Auto configuration works?
1. Triggered by @EnableAutoConfiguration which is included in @SpringBootApplication
2. Looks at classpath dependencies:
	- Which libraries are present (e.g JDBC, JPA, Web) 
	- Based on that, it decides what to configure
	Example:
		- If spring-mwebmvc is present configure Spring MVC
		- If HikariCP + JDBC -> configure DataSource
3. Uses Auto-Configuration classes 
 Spring boot loads configuration classes like: 
	- DataSourceAutoConfiguration
   	- WebMvcAutoConfiguration
	- HibernateJpaAutoConfiguration

These Classes are annotated with @Configuration, Define beans using @Bean

4. Loaded via metadata files
SpringBoot 3:
	META-INF/spring/org.spring.......

These files list all auto-configuration classes

5. Conditional annotation (core logic)
Auto-configuration works using condition like:

6. Back-off mechanism 
	- If you define your own bean Spring Boot backs off.
	Example: 
	@Bean
	public DataSource myDataSource() {...}
	Spring Boot will NOT create its default datasource.

In Short:
- Auto-Configuration in Spring Boot automatically configures beans based on classpath dependencies.
- It is enabled by @EnableAutoConfiguration and works by loading configuration classes defined in metadata files.
- These configurations use conditional annotations like @ConditionalOnClassand @ConditionalOnMissingBean 
  to decide whether to create beans.
- If the developer provides custom configuration, Spring Boot backs off
